//! YT strategies "ATH" (all-time-high close; not from a book): the team's AmiBroker AFLs in the `ATH/` folder of the AFL share,
//! built to `YT_STRATEGY_CODING_FLOW.md`. 233 sub-variants in 14 main variants (engines); the analysis is
//! `ATH/ATH_AFL_Variant_Analysis.md`, the reference files per sub-variant are `ATH/ATH_Variant_Reference_Sources.md`.
//!
//! This module lists the sub-variants, their rules (`rules`, `notes`) and the AFL's own parameters. The sub-variants listed by `ath_registry` run
//! on the Rust engine `ath_pctswing`, checked against the team's trade sheet (`ATH/verify/pctswing/RESULT.md`). For the others there is
//! no data source yet (the ATH database, NSE 500 cash and F&O stocks, daily bars, is added in a later phase) and no signal /
//! backtest code, so every sub-variant is `NotTestable`. Rules are written precisely in `note` and `rules` so the next phase
//! can implement them without re-reading the AFL. Conventions of the AFLs (nearly all of them): daily bars, long only unless
//! the rules say short, the all-time-high close is the highest close of all loaded bars before the signal bar
//! (`Ref(HHV(C, BarCount), -1)`), `ExRem` removes repeated signals, buys and sells are filled at the signal bar's close.
//!
//! This file is GENERATED by `scripts/ath_generate.py` from `ATH/ath_catalog.json`; change the catalog, not this file.
#![allow(dead_code)]
use crate::connors::{Ctx, ParamDef, Params, Status, StrategyDef, Trade};

